#====================================================================
# CMake dep_option 隐式关闭导致可选后端未编译（OHOS/交叉构建）
#====================================================================

id: E1093-cmake-dep-option-hidden-backend
draft: true
trigger_tool: cmake
phase: configuration, compilation, upstream-test
error_signature: TestVirtualJoystick failed|SDL_VIRTUAL_JOYSTICK=ON but resolved OFF|virtual joystick backend unavailable|SDL_HIDAPI=OFF
severity: 2
category: cmake, cross-compile, optional-backend, sdl2
match_keywords: dep_option, set_option, CMake option dependency, SDL_HIDAPI, SDL_VIRTUAL_JOYSTICK, optional backend, cache variable, feature probe, CTest
title: Prevent CMake dep_option from silently disabling an independently required test or runtime backend

root_cause: CMake dep_option(NAME ... PARENT OFF) does not behave like an independent boolean. When the parent option is OFF, CMake forces NAME OFF during configuration even if the caller supplies -DNAME=ON. A recipe that disables a hardware-facing provider (for example HIDAPI) can therefore suppress an otherwise independent virtual or test backend and produce a late upstream failure. The failure is easy to miss because compilation and version smoke tests still succeed.
affected_scope: Projects that model optional providers with CMake dependent options while a test backend, emulation backend, or software fallback is intended to remain independently selectable; especially cross-compiled packages where provider capability flags are intentionally reduced.

verification_cmd: cmake -S <source> -B <build> -DSDL_HIDAPI=OFF -DSDL_VIRTUAL_JOYSTICK=ON; cmake -LA -N <build>; ctest --test-dir <build> --output-on-failure
verification_evidence: In the SDL2 2.32.10 source snapshot (archive SHA-256 5f5993c530f084535c65a6879e9b26ad441169b3e25d789d83287040a9ca5165), the original dep_option resolved SDL_VIRTUAL_JOYSTICK=OFF when SDL_HIDAPI=OFF despite an explicit ON input. A bounded patch replaced only that declaration with set_option, preserving SDL_HIDAPI=OFF while resolving SDL_VIRTUAL_JOYSTICK=ON. The rebuilt testautomation executable passed TestVirtualJoystick 21/21, and the complete CTest inventory passed 16/16 (100%).

fix: Replace the dependent declaration only when the child backend has a valid implementation independent of the parent provider. Preserve the parent option value and avoid enabling unavailable hardware providers merely to satisfy a test. Add a configuration assertion for the resolved child value and retain the upstream test that exercises the backend.
negative_validation: Keep the unpatched source as a control and assert that SDL_HIDAPI=OFF plus SDL_VIRTUAL_JOYSTICK=ON resolves OFF. Treat a missing CTest executable as NOT_RUN rather than success; build the complete test target set before claiming the inventory pass rate.
safety_boundary: This pattern does not prove native device availability. A virtual or software backend validates feature wiring only; native GUI/audio claims still require their actual platform drivers and runtime evidence. Do not replace dep_option globally when the child genuinely requires the parent provider.

principles: P-CMAKE-OPTION-DEPENDENCY-001, P-UPSTREAM-TEST-INVENTORY-001
similar_to: [sdl2-version-smoke-does-not-prove-native-backends, sdl2-direct-production-tu-fixture-needs-public-include-root]
